WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.931
An exclusion says two conditions cannot hold together in the stated setting.

2
00:00:05.231 --> 00:00:07.855
Having one requires the absence of the other.

3
00:00:08.155 --> 00:00:10.480
No loaned sculpture is offered for sale.

4
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.465
Imagine a loaned sculpture.

5
00:00:12.765 --> 00:00:17.373
Offering it for sale would put it in the very combination the sentence excludes.

6
00:00:17.673 --> 00:00:19.380
So it is not offered for sale.

7
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.437
You can start from the other side too: a sculpture offered for sale cannot be loaned.

8
00:00:24.737 --> 00:00:28.705
Neither statement tells us that a loaned sculpture actually exists.

9
00:00:29.005 --> 00:00:32.397
An exclusion often supplies the negative link in a chain.

10
00:00:32.697 --> 00:00:40.804
It is easy to lose that link by reading no as an ordinary description of one case, or by turning not both into exactly one.

11
00:00:41.104 --> 00:00:44.752
Keep both whole ideas, including who or what they describe.

12
00:00:45.052 --> 00:00:49.895
Here the forbidden combination is loaned and offered for sale for the same sculpture.

13
00:00:50.195 --> 00:00:51.816
Ask what cannot coexist.

14
00:00:52.116 --> 00:00:59.476
If the sentence is a policy, keep the policy in the result: prohibited entry does not establish that nobody entered.

15
00:00:59.776 --> 00:01:04.043
If it is a descriptive rule, apply it as the stated factual guarantee.
